http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/series-events-afteranimate/\" target=\"_blank\">Show label after animate</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"series<errorbar>.events.afterAnimate","title":"afterAnimate","parent":"series<errorbar>-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"context":"Series"},{"name":"series<spline>-events--afterAnimate","returnType":"Function","since":"4.0","description":"Fires after the series has finished its initial animation, or in case animation is disabled, immediately as the series is displayed.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/series-events-afteranimate/\" target=\"_blank\">Show label after animate</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"series<spline>.events.afterAnimate","title":"afterAnimate","parent":"series<spline>-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"context":"Series"},{"name":"plotOptions-gauge-events--afterAnimate","returnType":"Function","since":"4.0","description":"Fires after the series has finished its initial animation, or in case animation is disabled, immediately as the series is displayed.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/series-events-afteranimate/\" target=\"_blank\">Show label after animate</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"plotOptions.gauge.events.afterAnimate","title":"afterAnimate","parent":"plotOptions-gauge-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"context":"Series"},{"name":"zAxis-events--afterBreaks","returnType":"Function","since":"4.1.0","description":"An event fired after the breaks have rendered.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/axisbreak/break-event//\" target=\"_blank\">afterBreak Event</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"zAxis.events.afterBreaks","title":"afterBreaks","parent":"zAxis-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"seeAlso":"<a href=\"#xAxis.breaks\">breaks</a>"},{"name":"xAxis-events--afterBreaks","returnType":"Function","since":"4.1.0","description":"An event fired after the breaks have rendered.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/axisbreak/break-event//\" target=\"_blank\">afterBreak Event</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"xAxis.events.afterBreaks","title":"afterBreaks","parent":"xAxis-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"seeAlso":"<a href=\"#xAxis.breaks\">breaks</a>"},{"name":"yAxis-events--afterBreaks","returnType":"Function","since":"4.1.0","description":"An event fired after the breaks have rendered.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/axisbreak/break-event//\" target=\"_blank\">afterBreak Event</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"yAxis.events.afterBreaks","title":"afterBreaks","parent":"yAxis-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"seeAlso":"<a href=\"#xAxis.breaks\">breaks</a>"},{"name":"chart-events--afterPrint","returnType":"Function","since":"4.1.0","description":"Fires after a chart is printed through the context menu item or the <code>Chart.print</code> method. Requires the exporting module.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/chart/events-beforeprint-afterprint/\" target=\"_blank\">Rescale the chart to print</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"chart.events.afterPrint","title":"afterPrint","parent":"chart-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"context":"Chart","defaults":"","values":"","seeAlso":""},{"name":"zAxis-events--afterSetExtremes","returnType":"Function","since":"2.3","description":"<p>As opposed to the <code>setExtremes</code> event, this event fires after the final min and max values are computed and corrected for <code>minRange</code>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fires when the minimum and maximum is set for the axis, either by calling the <code>.setExtremes()</code> method or by selecting an area in the chart. One parameter, <code>event</code>, is passed to the function. This contains common event information based on jQuery or MooTools depending on which library is used as the base for Highcharts.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The new user set minimum and maximum values can be found by <code>event.min</code> and <code>event.max</code>. These reflect the axis minimum and maximum in axis values. The actual data extremes are found in <code>event.dataMin</code> and <code>event.dataMax</code>.</p>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"zAxis.events.afterSetExtremes","title":"afterSetExtremes","parent":"zAxis-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"context":"Axis"},{"name":"yAxis-events--afterSetExtremes","returnType":"Function","since":"2.3","description":"<p>As opposed to the <code>setExtremes</code> event, this event fires after the final min and max values are computed and corrected for <code>minRange</code>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fires when the minimum and maximum is set for the axis, either by calling the <code>.setExtremes()</code> method or by selecting an area in the chart. One parameter, <code>event</code>, is passed to the function. This contains common event information based on jQuery or MooTools depending on which library is used as the base for Highcharts.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The new user set minimum and maximum values can be found by <code>event.min</code> and <code>event.max</code>. These reflect the axis minimum and maximum in axis values. The actual data extremes are found in <code>event.dataMin</code> and <code>event.dataMax</code>.</p>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"yAxis.events.afterSetExtremes","title":"afterSetExtremes","parent":"yAxis-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"context":"Axis"},{"name":"xAxis-events--afterSetExtremes","returnType":"Function","since":"2.3","description":"<p>As opposed to the <code>setExtremes</code> event, this event fires after the final min and max values are computed and corrected for <code>minRange</code>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fires when the minimum and maximum is set for the axis, either by calling the <code>.setExtremes()</code> method or by selecting an area in the chart. One parameter, <code>event</code>, is passed to the function. This contains common event information based on jQuery or MooTools depending on which library is used as the base for Highcharts.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The new user set minimum and maximum values can be found by <code>event.min</code> and <code>event.max</code>. These reflect the axis minimum and maximum in axis values. The actual data extremes are found in <code>event.dataMin</code> and <code>event.dataMax</code>.</p>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"xAxis.events.afterSetExtremes","title":"afterSetExtremes","parent":"xAxis-events","isParent":false,"products":[],"context":"Axis"},{"name":"zAxis-plotLines-label--align","returnType":"String","since":"2.1","description":"Horizontal alignment of the label. Can be one of \"left\", \"center\" or \"right\".","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/xaxis/plotlines-label-align-right/\" target=\"_blank\">Aligned to the right</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"zAxis.plotLines.label.align","title":"align","parent":"zAxis-plotLines-label","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"left"},{"name":"plotOptions-series-dataLabels--align","returnType":"String","description":"The alignment of the data label compared to the point.  If <code>right</code>, the right side of the label should be touching the point. For points with an extent, like columns, the alignments also dictates how to align it inside the box, as given with the <a href=\"#plotOptions.column.dataLabels.inside\">inside</a> option. Can be one of \"left\", \"center\" or \"right\".","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/series-datalabels-align-left/\" target=\"_blank\">Left aligned</a>.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/highcharts/72sbw0Lz/\">Understand alignment to boxes, lines and points</a>.","deprecated":false,"fullname":"plotOptions.series.dataLabels.align","title":"align","parent":"plotOptions-series-dataLabels","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"center","values":"[\"left\", \"center\", \"right\"]"},{"name":"xAxis-plotLines-label--align","returnType":"String","since":"2.1","description":"Horizontal alignment of the label. Can be one of \"left\", \"center\" or \"right\".","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/xaxis/plotlines-label-align-right/\" target=\"_blank\">Aligned to the right</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"xAxis.plotLines.label.align","title":"align","parent":"xAxis-plotLines-label","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"left"},{"name":"xAxis-labels--align","returnType":"String","description":"What part of the string the given position is anchored to. If <code>left</code>, the left side of the string is at the axis position. Can be one of <code>\"left\"</code>, <code>\"center\"</code> or <code>\"right\"</code>. Defaults to an intelligent guess based on which side of the chart the axis is on and the rotation of the label.","demo":"Align <a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/xaxis/labels-align-left/\" target=\"_blank\">left</a> and, \r\n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/xaxis/labels-align-right/\" target=\"_blank\">right</a> on X axis.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/highcharts/72sbw0Lz/\">Understand alignment to boxes, lines and points</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"xAxis.labels.align","title":"align","parent":"xAxis-labels","isParent":false,"products":[],"values":"[\"left\", \"center\", \"right\"]"},{"name":"series<column>-dataLabels--align","returnType":"String","description":"The alignment of the data label compared to the point.  If <code>right</code>, the right side of the label should be touching the point. For points with an extent, like columns, the alignments also dictates how to align it inside the box, as given with the <a href=\"#plotOptions.column.dataLabels.inside\">inside</a> option. Can be one of \"left\", \"center\" or \"right\".","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/series-datalabels-align-left/\" target=\"_blank\">Left aligned</a>.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/highcharts/72sbw0Lz/\">Understand alignment to boxes, lines and points</a>.","deprecated":false,"fullname":"series<column>.dataLabels.align","title":"align","parent":"series<column>-dataLabels","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"center","values":"[\"left\", \"center\", \"right\"]"},{"name":"yAxis-labels--align","returnType":"String","description":"What part of the string the given position is anchored to.  Can be one of <code>\"left\"</code>, <code>\"center\"</code> or <code>\"right\"</code>. The exact position also depends on the <code>labels.x</code> setting. Angular gauges and solid gauges defaults to <code>center</code>.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/labels-align-left/\" target=\"_blank\">\"left\"</a> on Y axis","deprecated":false,"fullname":"yAxis.labels.align","title":"align","parent":"yAxis-labels","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"right","values":"[\"left\", \"center\", \"right\"]"},{"name":"zAxis-plotBands-label--align","returnType":"String","since":"2.1","description":"Horizontal alignment of the label. Can be one of \"left\", \"center\" or \"right\".","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/xaxis/plotbands-label-align/\" target=\"_blank\">Aligned to the right<