yle","title":"menuItemHoverStyle","parent":"navigation","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"{ \"background\": \"#335cad\", \"color\": \"#ffffff\" }","seeAlso":"In <a href=\"http://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-design-and-style/style-by-css\">styled mode</a>, the menu items are styled with the <code>.highcharts-menu-item</code> class."},{"name":"navigation--menuItemStyle","returnType":"CSSObject","since":"2.0","description":"CSS styles for the individual items within the popup menu appearing by  default when the export icon is clicked. The menu items are rendered in HTML.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/navigation/menuitemstyle/\" target=\"_blank\">Add a grey stripe to the left</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"navigation.menuItemStyle","title":"menuItemStyle","parent":"navigation","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"{ \"padding\": \"0.5em 1em\", \"color\": \"#333333\", \"background\": \"none\" }","seeAlso":"In <a href=\"http://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-design-and-style/style-by-css\">styled mode</a>, the menu items are styled with the <code>.highcharts-menu-item</code> class."},{"name":"exporting-buttons-contextButton--menuItems","returnType":"Array<Object>","since":"2.0","description":"<p>A collection of config options for the menu items. Each options object consists\r of a <code>text</code> option which is a string to show in the menu item, as\r well as an <code>onclick</code> parameter which is a callback function to run\r on click.</p>\r <p>By default, there is the \"Print\" menu item plus one menu item for each of the available export types.\r Menu items can be customized by defining a new array of items and assigning \r <code>null</code> to unwanted positions (see override example below).</p>","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/exporting/buttons-contextbutton-onclick/\" target=\"_blank\">Skip the menu and export the chart directly</a>,\r\n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/exporting/buttons-contextbutton-menuitems/\" target=\"_blank\">override the menu items</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"exporting.buttons.contextButton.menuItems","title":"menuItems","parent":"exporting-buttons-contextButton","isParent":false,"products":[],"seeAlso":""},{"name":"navigation--menuStyle","returnType":"CSSObject","since":"2.0","description":"CSS styles for the popup menu appearing by default when the export icon is clicked. This menu is rendered in HTML.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/navigation/menustyle/\" target=\"_blank\">Light gray menu background</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"navigation.menuStyle","title":"menuStyle","parent":"navigation","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"{ \"border\": \"1px solid #999999\", \"background\": \"#ffffff\", \"padding\": \"5px 0\" }","seeAlso":"In <a href=\"http://www.highcharts.com/docs/chart-design-and-style/style-by-css\">styled mode</a>, the menu is styled with the <code>.highcharts-menu</code> class."},{"name":"xAxis--min","returnType":"Number","description":"The minimum value of the axis. If <code>null</code> the min value is automatically calculated. If the <code>startOnTick</code> option is true, the <code>min</code> value might be rounded down.","demo":"Y axis min of <a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/min-startontick-false/\" target=\"_blank\">-50 with startOnTick to false</a>,\n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/min-startontick-true/\" target=\"_blank\">-50 with startOnTick true by default</a>","fullname":"xAxis.min","title":"min","parent":"xAxis","isParent":false,"products":[]},{"name":"zAxis--min","returnType":"Number","description":"The minimum value of the axis. If <code>null</code> the min value is automatically calculated. If the <code>startOnTick</code> option is true, the <code>min</code> value might be rounded down.","demo":"Y axis min of <a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/min-startontick-false/\" target=\"_blank\">-50 with startOnTick to false</a>,\n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/min-startontick-true/\" target=\"_blank\">-50 with startOnTick true by default</a>","fullname":"zAxis.min","title":"min","parent":"zAxis","isParent":false,"products":[]},{"name":"yAxis--min","returnType":"Number","description":"<p>The minimum value of the axis. If <code>null</code> the min value is automatically calculated.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If the <code>startOnTick</code> option is true (default), the <code>min</code> value might be rounded down.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The automatically calculated minimum value is also affected by <a href=\"#yAxis.floor\">floor</a>, <a href=\"#yAxis.softMin\">softMin</a>, <a href=\"#yAxis.minPadding\">minPadding</a>, <a href=\"#yAxis.minRange\">minRange</a> as well as <a href=\"#plotOptions.series.threshold\">series.threshold</a> and <a href=\"#plotOptions.series.softThreshold\">series.softThreshold</a>.</p>","demo":"Y axis min of <a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/min-startontick-false/\" target=\"_blank\">-50 with startOnTick to false</a>,\r\n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/min-startontick-true/\" target=\"_blank\">-50 with startOnTick true by default</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"yAxis.min","title":"min","parent":"yAxis","isParent":false,"products":[]},{"name":"yAxis--minColor","returnType":"Color","since":"4.0","description":"Solid gauge only. Unless <a href=\"#yAxis.stops\">stops</a> are set, the color to represent the minimum value of the Y axis.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/mincolor-maxcolor/\" target=\"_blank\">Min and max color</a>","deprecated":false,"fullname":"yAxis.minColor","title":"minColor","parent":"yAxis","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"#e6ebf5"},{"name":"responsive-rules-condition--minHeight","returnType":"Number","since":"5.0.0","description":"The responsive rule applies if the chart height is greater than this.","demo":"","deprecated":false,"fullname":"responsive.rules.condition.minHeight","title":"minHeight","parent":"responsive-rules-condition","isParent":false,"products":[],"context":"","defaults":"0","values":"","seeAlso":""},{"name":"xAxis--minPadding","returnType":"Number","since":"1.2.0","description":"Padding of the min value relative to the length of the axis. A padding of 0.05 will make a 100px axis 5px longer. This is useful when you don't want the lowest data value to appear on the edge of the plot area. When the axis' <code>min</code> option is set or a min extreme is set using <code>axis.setExtremes()</code>, the minPadding will be ignored.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/minpadding/\" target=\"_blank\">Min padding of 0.2</a>","fullname":"xAxis.minPadding","title":"minPadding","parent":"xAxis","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"0.01"},{"name":"yAxis--minPadding","returnType":"Number","since":"1.2.0","description":"Padding of the min value relative to the length of the axis. A padding of 0.05 will make a 100px axis 5px longer. This is useful when you don't want the lowest data value to appear on the edge of the plot area.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/yaxis/minpadding/\" target=\"_blank\">Min paddi