:"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/column-pointpadding-default/\" target=\"_blank\">0.1 by default</a>, \n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/column-pointpadding-025/\" target=\"_blank\">0.25</a>, \n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/column-pointpadding-none/\" target=\"_blank\">0 for tightly packed columns</a>,","fullname":"series<boxplot>.pointPadding","title":"pointPadding","parent":"series<boxplot>","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"0.1"},{"name":"series<columnrange>--pointPadding","returnType":"Number","description":"Padding between each column or bar, in x axis units.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/column-pointpadding-default/\" target=\"_blank\">0.1 by default</a>, \n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/column-pointpadding-025/\" target=\"_blank\">0.25</a>, \n\t\t\t<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/column-pointpadding-none/\" target=\"_blank\">0 for tightly packed columns</a>,","fullname":"series<columnrange>.pointPadding","title":"pointPadding","parent":"series<columnrange>","isParent":false,"products":[],"defaults":"0.1"},{"name":"series<areasplinerange>--pointPlacement","returnType":"String|Number","since":"2.3.0","description":"<p>Possible values: <code>null</code>, <code>\"on\"</code>, <code>\"between\"</code>.</p>\r\n<p>In a column chart, when pointPlacement is <code>\"on\"</code>, the point will not create any padding of the X axis. In a polar column chart this means that the first column points directly north. If the pointPlacement is <code>\"between\"</code>, the columns will be laid out between ticks. This is useful for example for visualising an amount between two points in time or in a certain sector of a polar chart.</p>\r\n<p>Since Highcharts 3.0.2, the point placement can also be numeric, where 0 is on the axis value, -0.5 is between this value and the previous, and 0.5 is between this value and the next. Unlike the textual options, numeric point placement options won't affect axis padding.</p>\r\n<p>Note that pointPlacement needs a <a href=\"#plotOptions.series.pointRange\">pointRange</a> to work. For column series this is computed, but for line-type series it needs to be set.</p>\r\n<p>Defaults to <code>null</code> in cartesian charts, <code>\"between\"</code> in polar charts.","demo":"<a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/series-pointplacement-between/\" target=\"_blank\">Between in a column chart</a>, <a href=\"http://jsfiddle.net/gh/get/library/pure/highcharts/highcharts/tree/master/samples/highcharts/plotoptions/series-pointplacement-numeric/\" target=\"_blank\">numeric placement for custom layout</a>.","deprecated":false,"fullname":"series<areasplinerange>.pointPlacement","title":"pointPlacement","parent":"series<areasplinerange>","isParent":false,"products":[],"values":"[null, \"on\", \"between\"]","seeAlso":"<a href=\"#xAxis.tickmarkPlacement\">xAxis.tickmarkPlacement</a>"},{"name":"plotOptions-areasplinerange--pointPlacement","returnType":"String|Number","since":"2.3.0","description":"<p>Possible values: <code>null</code>, <code>\"on\"</code>, <code>\"between\"</code>.</p>\r\n<p>In a column chart, when pointPlacement is <code>\"on\"</code>, the point will not create any padding of the X axis. In a polar column chart this means that the first column points directly north. If the pointPlacement is <code>\"between\"</code>, the columns will be laid out between ticks. This is useful for example for visualising an 